
1.To Import the New Maven Project =====================================================>

Step 1 : Right Click in the Project Explorer tab -> New -> Project -> Maven -> Maven Project -> Browse -> Select the Project (Eg : E:\ProjectCpy\Projects-main\demo) -> Click Next. 


Step 2 : Eclipse IDE – New Maven Project – Select an Archetype window.

In the Filter box, type:

maven-archetype-quickstart

Then select:

*Group Id: org.apache.maven.archetypes

*Artifact Id: maven-archetype-quickstart

*Version: Select the latest available version.


Step 3 : Click Next

On the next screen, fill in these details:

Field   :       What to enter

Group Id    -   com.example

Artifact Id -   MyFirstProject

Version     -   1.0-SNAPSHOT

Package     -   com.example

Step 4 : Click Finish, Eclipse will create your Maven project.

You should then see:

src/main/java – Your Java source code.

src/test/java – Your test files.

pom.xml – Maven dependencies and configuration.



~ To Run the Project.

Step 1 : Right Click on the "Project Name" -> Run as -> Maven Build -> Goals (Type): clean install -> Check in Console : BUILD SUCCESS.
Step 2 : Right Click on the  "src/main/java" -> Run as -> Java Application.



FYI -

 ~ Use maven-archetype-quickstart for a basic Java Maven project.
